This design is sparse. Every teacher rated 5 essays, but 435 of the 881 essays were rated by a single teacher, and only 50 by four or more. Essays and teachers are crossed in the model, but most essay–teacher pairs were never observed; the components rest on the essays that more than one teacher rated, and on each teacher's five essays.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="show"}
# The default optimizer stops just short of lme4's convergence tolerance on this
# fit; bobyqa converges and gives the same estimates to three decimals.
fit_es <- lmer(form, data = es, control = lmerControl(optimizer = "bobyqa"))
vc_es <- components(fit_es, sub("t x r", "c x r", sub("task", "criterion", labels)))
vc_es
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
<div class="kable-table">

